[rgg@cs.mu.oz.au (Rupert G. Goldie) writes:]
[] How can I attract more monsters when I'm on the first few levels ?
[] I have great  difficulty trying to find enough monsters to kill to
[] satisfy the two times level rule. Do I just have to wait for ages
[] or are there ways of attracting monsters ?

play with the "time" option on so you can keep track of critical
events.  there's no normal way to force monster generation, you
just have to wait.  exceptions are when you have a wand/scroll of
create monster, encounter a magic trap, find a bag of tricks, or
do something at a sink or fountain that attracts a monster.  the
two times level rule is really a rule-of-thumb, don't die for it!
i find that on occasion i may leave level 1 with ~15 Hp's (for
example) knowing that the next goblin killed will put me over the
limit for a level 2 character and so on.  your intent by using this
rule is to prevent a too rapid descent wherein you find yourself
facing monsters much tougher than you.  a level 5 character on dlev
5 is barely viable, in my opinion.  your mileage may vary ...

